  "additionalProperties": false,
  "description": "Return the complete assessment, issues and questions arrays. APPROVE requires no issues/questions and every change supported and every retrieval gap explicitly nonmaterial. REJECT requires an actionable code issue; material questions remain blocking even with REJECT. HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED needs an explicit question or unresolved change/gap. Code issue: description, supplied evidence references, current code location and actionable suggestion. Context question: exactly what is missing, why it matters and source/schema retrieval kind; no invented code defect/location. Cite E IDs, optionally with character start/end for text entries; RDF_FACT references cite the whole atomic fact. Software extracts exact text. Never reproduce quotations unless deliberately asserting one (optional quote is checked exactly). Locations contain start/end, optional unit (default lines); software binds current hashes and extracts code. Regulation establishes obligations. Schema/declared representation establishes RDF identifiers, paths, datatypes and units. Approved research scope establishes the external population assumption. A regulation need not literally contain an RDF IRI. Mappings do not establish regulatory formulas or compliance answers. Genuine missing/contradictory mappings stay questions. Citations do not prove interpretation. When supplied, assess every change ID once, including removed/replaced constraints and their reachable enforcement. REGRESSION must link the zero-based issue index; UNRESOLVED stays blocking. For APPROVE assess every gap ID with material=false and why; material gaps require questions. Software maintains stable issue IDs, prior reconciliation and candidate bindings. Review all supplied prior issues; APPROVE asserts none remains. Do not return hashes, issue IDs, reconciliation states, source-clause echoes or duplicate removal assessments. Never request evaluation fixtures/labels/solutions."
